{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-embeddable-cardinality-vs-energy","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:embeddable-cardinality-vs-energy","kind":"remark","title":"Overlap weighting changes energy, not channel count","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-embeddable-knot-operator"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-embeddable-knot-operator","tags":["cardinality","bond-order","overlap-weight","N2","active-set"],"text":"embeddable-cardinality-vs-energy.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:embeddable-cardinality-vs-energy\"></a><p><em>Overlap weighting changes only the energy, never the channel count. Every channel with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">w > 0</code> is occupied, so the active-set cardinality (the bond order of <a href=\"#prop:co-lp-dual-binding\" data-at=\"molecular-construction/co-computation\">the CO LP dual</a>) is independent of the weights. The equal-channel model (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">w \\equiv 1</code>) overbinds: for the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma + 2\\pi</code> triple bond it gives <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1.42\\times</code> the observed <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">D_0(\\mathrm{N_2})</code>. A lateral weight <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">w_\\perp \\in [0.3, 0.7]</code> brackets it (witness <code>embeddable-knot-operator</code>).</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/embeddable-cardinality-vs-energy.md","heading":"Remark","number":"18.5.8","page":"b/rem-embeddable-cardinality-vs-energy","qa":{"counts":{"pass":60,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":0},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
